# RFC 2180:
# 4.2.1 If the ".SILENT" suffix is used, and the STORE completed
#       successfully for all the non-expunged messages, the server SHOULD
#       return a tagged OK.
depends 2180base
send 1
a store 1:2 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 1
a OK done
send 1
a uid expunge 1:2
receive 3
* 1 EXPUNGE
* 1 EXPUNGE
a OK done
use watcher
# main expunged 1:2 above, which took a modseq, so .silent no longer
# lines up with what this session has reported and the store is echoed
# back. Sending too much is better than too little, so expect it.
send 1
a store 1:3 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 2
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 FLAGS (\Deleted))
a OK done
# RFC 2180:
# 4.2.2. If the ".SILENT" suffix is not used, and only expunged messages
#        are referenced, the server SHOULD return only a tagged NO.
send 1
a store 1:2 -flags \deleted
receive 1
a NO Cannot store on expunged messages
# 4.2.3. If the ".SILENT" suffix is not used, and a mixture of expunged
#        and non-expunged messages are referenced, the server MAY set the
#        flags and return a FETCH response for the non-expunged messages
#        along with a tagged NO. ugle is new to the mailbox, so the
#        flag list is re-announced first.
send 1
a store 1:3 +flags ugle
receive 4
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen ugle)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen ugle \*)] permanent flags
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 FLAGS (\Deleted ugle))
a NO Cannot store on expunged messages
end
